      "text": "First, complete the table to find the difference in costs.\n\nUS dollar = 7.00Namibian = 6.00Chinese $\\frac{US\\ dollar}{X}$ = 105.00Namibia $1 Dollar = 7.00$Namibian Xdollars $\\frac{7}{6}Dollars= 105$Namibia $\\frac{6}{7}Dollars =XDollars$ $\\frac{1}{6}Dollars = \\frac{1}{7}$Namibian $1Dollars= \\frac{1}{6}Dollars \\times 7$Namibian =1.195XChinese  \n105.00Namibia/1.195Chinese = 87.47 Chinese Yuan[as the problem states that Chinese Yuan = 105Namibian]\n\nThus, the answer is \\boxed{87}. Let's carefully solve the given problem step-by-step.\n\n1. **Understand the Conversion Factors:**\n    - 1 US dollar (USD) = 7 Namibian dollars (NAD)\n    - 1 US dollar (USD) = 6 Chinese yuan (CNY)\n\n2. **Given Data:**\n    - The cost of the painting in Namibian dollars (NAD) is 105 NAD.\n\n3. **Objective:**\n    - Convert the cost of the painting from Namibian dollars to Chinese yuan.\n\n4. **Convert Namibian Dollars to U.S. Dollars:**\n    - From the conversion factor, 1 US dollar = 7 Namibian dollars.\n    - Therefore to find the cost in US dollars, we divide 105 NAD by 7.\n    \\[\n    105 \\text{ NAD} \\div 7 = 15 \\text{ US dollars}\n    \\]\n\n5. **Convert US Dollars to Chinese Yuan:**\n    - From the conversion factor, 1 US dollar = 6 Chinese yuan.\n    - So to find the cost in Chinese yuan, we multiply 15 US dollars by 6.\n    \\[\n    15 \\text{ US dollars} \\times 6 \\text{ CNY/US dollar} = 90 \\text{ CNY}\n    \\]\n\n6. **Conclusion:**\n    - The painting costs 90 Chinese yuan.\n\nHence, the final answer is \\boxed{90}.",
